Description: Kintrinsic for Linux — guardian-chartered device warden
 charterd is the privileged broker spine: it verifies guardian-signed
 grants and enforces schedule/budget limits, app-install brokering, and
 execution lockdown. Works standalone via device-only limits (set in
 the Screen Time settings app, no phone needed). Ships the systemd
 service, D-Bus policy, polkit rules, fapolicyd policy, noexec mount
 units, the charter CLI, charter-lock, charter-xclients,
 charter-settings, charter-setup and charter-applock. Run
 'charter-setup <user>' to lock down an account. fapolicyd is
 installed but stays off until 'charter-applock arm' is run.

